there's so much to talk about with when  it comes to the finale so if you don't  mind i'll just kind of dive in  and ask you about killing tracy and  gordon  yeah that was a big deal um we spent a  lot of time  uh puzzling that through in the writers  room you know we  had come up with this we would set all  the pieces in place  and were trying to decide how they were  going to play themselves out and there  were certainly  various characters were in jeopardy in  various different ways  and as we started talking about the  possibility of having  one or both either gordo or tracy take  that last run then you start talking  about whether  they should die and would one of them  die would both of them die  and we went round and round on it for a  while internally  and ultimately i think what carried the  day was just  our sense that this was the right ending  to their story as  characters that it felt like we had  taken them on a journey  uh from season one and shown you how  they  first met then the tre you know then the  troubles in their marriage  then tracy gets this opportunity how  that affects gordo's life then they  split between the seasons  and the two of them coming back together  on the moon  and finding each other finally at the  very end and then  dying together in this heroic endeavor  seemed like  the right way to end their story and  even though we were  sort of all heartbroken about it because  we love the characters and we love the  cast members you know  we love sarah sarah and michael and it  was hard but um  at the end we just sort of felt like it  was the right thing to do and it felt  like  that's that's the satisfying ending to  the story of tracy and gordo  now was this a situation where you knew  that the you knew that the actors  wouldn't be  available for season three and then so  it was kind of a way of  writing writing towards that or did you  decide  the opposite way it was the opposite i  mean they were available we  we could have continued both characters  and we had plans you know we had  preliminary plans you know  because we had sort of sketched ahead  multiple seasons in the show and  we started ideas about what we were  going to do with them in the third  season  but um the story just sort of took us  there so it really wasn't about  actor availability at all it must be  nice to have that kind of freedom within  the writers room  it is it's great you know i mean it's  it's a very open very free room and i i  always try to tell my writing staffs  come up with the idea that's crazy come  up with something that's shocking you  know say this say the thing that you  don't think you can say and let's  you know most of the time you're not  going to do it you know a lot of the  times you're just going to ask  that's too much but sometimes it is the  right move and sometimes when somebody  says it  everybody came and takes a step back and  goes oh i don't know if we can do that  and then you start talking it through  and you start seeing the opportunities  and the possibilities  and then you shy away from it and then  you just keep finding yourself like  like a gravitational force coming back  to it so we literally it was pitched out  early  and then you know gordon tracy could die  when they go on that run  and we all went ah no let's not do that  but it just kept coming back up it just  it would not the idea wouldn't die in  the writer's room and we just kept  coming back to it until it was clear  that  it was just the right place to go gotcha  so in terms of leaping forward to 1994  for season three you know we saw in the  leap from season one to season two that  you know you we get we get some of the  details about what happened between in  those years  that gets skipped over but not a lot and  they kind of trickle in  is that is that similar to the approach  we're taking for season three  yeah it'll be a very similar approach we  want to you know  let the audience be surprised by the  changes of what's happened where the  characters are in their lives  what's happened in the world and then  give them a certain sort of framework of  okay here's some historical events and  some cultural events that happened in  between the two seasons  but then as the season goes on you keep  making references to things that  happened in the intervening years  there's things that are on television  there's things in newspapers there's  like casual lines that are thrown out  little easter eggs along the way  you know apple has also had this uh as  part of the platform  you know we had certain bonus uh pieces  that that we put in there that also  filled in there were news broadcasts  there were sort of confessionals there  were  you know other historical pieces that we  put on the platform for people that were  really really interested  in those alternate history ideas you  know what else because we  worked out a lot of that stuff so here  it is if you're interested  here's another way to go experience that  yeah i mean  it's actually funny uh i i remembered  recently the very first set visit for  the show that i ever got to do  uh before it had ever come out and i  asked you  uh about you know what's the divergent  point what what is the one thing that  happened that led to  the russians beating the americans to  the moon and you  you said what it was there and i'm not  mentioning it now just because a it  might have changed in the years  but be you i don't think we've we've had  that been revealed on the show  and i was curious like is that something  you ever do plan to reveal  oh uh i know what you're talking about  and actually yeah it's just  uh it's it it's not a huge player i'll  just give it to you know the our point  of divergence was the idea that sergey  korlov who was the father of the soviet  space program  uh in reality he died during  an operation in moscow in the mid 60s  and  after that point like their moon program  really never  pulled together like they developed the  in one rocket but it kept blowing up and  it just it kind of  it all kind of fell apart in the race to  the moon and our point of divergence was  that  corelog lives and that somehow he was  able to pull all the bureaucratic pieces  together and the technological  challenges  and he kind of made their moon landing  happen that was the point of divergence  for us  we had always sort of tried to figure  out a way to mention it  but it never quite there was never like  an organic  easy way to sort of casually say that  somebody did not die in an operation  you know so we never quite figured out a  way to really  cement that into the story and um  i think we had we we might have  mentioned the name corelog in dialogue  somewhere or maybe  that got dropped out but it's kind of  one of those things i think we've  sort of forgotten because it's so far  now in the past of of our creative  process that we haven't ever actually  kind of pinpointed it on camera that  that's the point of divergence  in terms of season three what else do  you feel comfortable teasing at this  point  well you know just that not much just  that it's it jumps does jump to the 90s  and mars is clearly you know a big focus  of  what season three is about and uh the  rest of it you know we're just kind of  keeping under wraps for now  the season two flash forward that  happens at the end of season one  we do see that scene in the context of  season two but it's you know  it's not the kickoff point for season  two it's kind of deep into the middle of  the season  is that similar to how is that is the  mars landing that we see  at in the teas for at the end of season  two a similar approach  uh i'd rather not say that's right one  thing i do want to make sure i ask about  uh getting nirvana uh for the final  moments was that  as hard as you might have expected or to  come together pretty easily  i can't you know it's just a question of  money ain't cheap  i'll put it that way but none of the big  songs are cheap so  we've you know we've used everyone from  sinatra to nirvana to the rolling stones  and ac dc at this point so  we we kind of know what we're in for and  we budget accordingly  well that's my time with you thank you  so much and uh  can't wait for season three good luck  with it great thank you very much

